{"id":"h13t3","name":"Golden Customer Record","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>customer_updates</b> has the columns <code>update_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>updated_at</code> (timestamp), <code>email</code>, <code>phone</code> and <code>city</code>. Each row is a <b>partial</b> update sent by one of our apps:</p>\n<ul><li>a field that is <code>NULL</code> means <i>not changed</i> by this update;</li>\n<li>a field that is not <code>NULL</code> replaces the previous value, even when it is an empty or blank string: that means the value was <b>cleared</b>.</li></ul>\n<p>Updates are applied in order of <code>updated_at</code>, then <code>update_id</code>. The current value of a field is therefore the latest non-<code>NULL</code> value sent for it, then cleaned:</p>\n<ul><li><code>email</code>: trimmed and lower case;</li>\n<li><code>phone</code>: digits only (every other character removed);</li>\n<li><code>city</code>: trimmed, with the first letter of each word in upper case and the others in lower case (<code>INITCAP</code>).</li></ul>\n<p>A value that is empty after cleaning is <code>NULL</code> in the result (cleared). A field never sent is <code>NULL</code> too.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per customer with the columns <code>customer_id</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>phone</code>, <code>city</code>, <code>last_update</code> (the latest <code>updated_at</code>) and <code>updates</code> (number of rows), sorted by <code>customer_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>customer_updates</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>update_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>updated_at</th><th>email</th><th>phone</th><th>city</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>10</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td> Amina@Mail.COM </td><td>+212 6-12-34</td><td>casablanca</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>10</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>  rabat </td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>10</td><td>2026-03-02 10:00:00</td><td></td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>11</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>k@x.io</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>11</td><td>2026-03-02 08:30:00</td><td>null</td><td>06 00</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>11</td><td>2026-03-02 08:30:00</td><td>null</td><td>07 11</td><td>EL JADIDA</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>12</td><td>2026-03-02 08:10:00</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>email</th><th>phone</th><th>city</th><th>last_update</th><th>updates</th></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>null</td><td>21261234</td><td>Rabat</td><td>2026-03-02 10:00:00</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>k@x.io</td><td>0600</td><td>El Jadida</td><td>2026-03-02 08:30:00</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>null</td><td>2026-03-02 08:10:00</td><td>1</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>customer_updates</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>customer_id</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>phone</code>, <code>city</code>, <code>last_update</code>, <code>updates</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["dernière valeur non nulle","array_agg FILTER","NULL vs chaîne vide","nettoyage","regexp_replace"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>customer_updates</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>customer_id</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>phone</code>, <code>city</code>, <code>last_update</code>, <code>updates</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ HH:MM:SS pour une date avec heure.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"customer_updates":{"columns":[["update_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["updated_at","TIMESTAMP"],["email","TEXT"],["phone","TEXT"],["city","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,10,"2026-03-02 08:00:00"," Amina@Mail.COM ","+212 6-12-34","casablanca"],[2,10,"2026-03-02 09:00:00",null,null,"  rabat "],[3,10,"2026-03-02 10:00:00","",null,null],[4,11,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","k@x.io",null,null],[6,11,"2026-03-02 08:30:00",null,"06 00",null],[5,11,"2026-03-02 08:30:00",null,"07 11","EL JADIDA"],[7,12,"2026-03-02 08:10:00",null,null,null]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","email","phone","city","last_update","updates"],"rows":[[10,null,"21261234","Rabat","2026-03-02 10:00:00",3],[11,"k@x.io","0600","El Jadida","2026-03-02 08:30:00",3],[12,null,null,null,"2026-03-02 08:10:00",1]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"customer_updates":{"columns":[["update_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["updated_at","TIMESTAMP"],["email","TEXT"],["phone","TEXT"],["city","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","a@b.c","1","fès"],[2,1,"2026-03-02 08:05:00","   ","n/a",null],[3,1,"2026-03-02 08:09:00",null,null,"  "]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","email","phone","city","last_update","updates"],"rows":[[1,null,null,null,"2026-03-02 08:09:00",3]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}